==Trivia==
[[File:JN133 AS.png|thumb|175px|The "[[After the Story]]" artwork for this episode]]
* [[Get Inspired! Let's Solve a Poké Riddle!!]]: {{p|Azumarill}}
** The [https://twitter.com/anipoke_PR/status/1596413446567784448 riddle] and the [https://twitter.com/anipoke_PR/status/1596783385090744320 answer] were only posted on the official [https://twitter.com/anipoke_PR anipoke_PR] Twitter account.
* This episode, along with [[JN134|the next episode]], takes place during the same time as the events of ''[[JN129|A Flood of Torrential Gains!]]'' to ''[[JN132|Partners in Time!]]''.
* [[Goh]] reads out the [[title card]] for this episode.
* This is the first episode to air in Japan after the release of [[Pokémon Scarlet and Violet]].
** This also marks the first time when a [[series]] in the {{pkmn|animated series}} does not conclude within the [[generation|generation(s)]] it focuses on.
** After the airing of the episode, a [[Team Rocket Expedition which stands by the evils of love and truth|short]] where {{TRT}} interacts with a {{p|Sprigatito}} was shown, marking the first appearance of a [[Generation IX]] Pokémon and the first mention of [[Paldea]] in the animated series.
* This is the second main series episode where {{Ash}} and {{AP|Pikachu}} don’t appear in any capacity (not counting the recap in the beginning of the episode), after ''[[JN032|Time After Time!]]''.
* As of this episode, all [[Project Mew]] Chasers have been revealed to own a [[Legendary Pokémon]].
* This marks the first time a [[Generation V]] Legendary Pokémon has received a [[Pokédex entry]] in the animated series.
* This episode marks the first appearance of several Pokémon species in the main series after long absences:
** {{p|Lileep}}, who last appeared in ''[[DP017|Wild in the Streets!]]'', 735 episodes earlier.
** {{p|Cranidos}}, who last appeared in ''[[DP050|Tag! We're It...!]]'', 702 episodes earlier.
** {{p|Carbink}}, who last appeared in ''[[XY131|Down to the Fiery Finish!]]'', 288 episodes earlier.
** {{p|Tyrunt}}, who last appeared in ''[[XY140|Till We Compete Again!]]'', 279 episodes earlier.
* The cavern beneath [[Faraway Island]] is highly similar to the [[Tree of Beginning]] from ''[[M08|Lucario and the Mystery of Mew]]''. Both are extremely isolated locations where a {{an|Mew}} can be found, with unusual plant life and numerous [[Fossil|Fossil Pokémon]] living within them. They are also both guarded by [[Generation III]] Legendary Pokémon.
* This is the only episode of the English dub of [[Pokémon the Series|''Pokémon the Series'']] that [[Sarah Natochenny]] was not a cast member for after [[AG146|her debut]].
* Goh's sensor device resembles a [[Game Boy Advance]], with the light on top of it resembling an inserted game cartridge. The light being green could also be a reference to {{game|Emerald}}, which is the only game to feature Faraway Island.
* The [[Who's That Pokémon?|Dare da?]] segment is replaced with [[eyecatch]]es of Ash, Goh, and Pikachu for this episode.
* [[Professor Amaranth]], {{an|Mew}}, {{Gary}}, [[Horace]], [[Danika]], [[Quillon]], Goh, and {{TP|Goh|Grookey}} narrate the preview of the [[JN134|next episode]].

